{
  "policy_type": "rules",
  "name": "policy_ep_40",
  "rules": [
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vy", "op": "<", "value": -0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": ">", "value": -0.1},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": "<", "value": 0.1}
      ],
      "then": 2
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vx", "op": ">", "value": 0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": "<", "value": 0.1}
      ],
      "then": 3
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vx", "op": "<", "value": -0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": ">", "value": -0.1}
      ],
      "then": 1
    },
    {
      "if": [
        {"feature": "vy", "op": ">", "value": -0.5},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": "<", "value": -0.1},
        {"feature": "theta", "op": ">", "value": 0.1}
      ],
      "then": 2
    }
  ],
  "default_action": 0,
  "notes": "This new policy is influenced by the need to improve the agent's performance in landing safely while minimizing tilt and descent speed. The rules prioritize firing the main engine when vertical velocity is low and the lander is stable, which is crucial for successful landings. Additionally, the orientation engines are activated when horizontal velocity is high, ensuring better control of the lander's angle. These adjustments were made based on the observation of previous trajectories where maintaining stability during descent was critical for success, particularly focusing on the conditions under which agents crashed or achieved successful landings."
}

